why isn't the best scene in dr strange  in the multiverse of madness the one you  think it is because the real best scene  plays into director sam raimi's biggest  strengths keep watching be warned that  spoilers are ahead it's been six years  since benedict cumberbatch first donned  the cloak of levitation as the master of  the mystic arts and director scott  derrickson's doctor strange since then  he's helped save the world from thanos  in avengers infinity war and end game  before cleaning up peter parker's  multiversal mess in spider-man and no  way home  thank you steven but the sorcerer has  finally returned for his own sequel dr  strange in the multiverse of madness in  which he explores different universes  while trying to help america chavez  escape a deadly threat it's impressive  how much director sam raimi's multiverse  of madness manages to pull off in its  two hours and seven minutes considering  it has so many key players and ideas to  establish not only does it boldly make  former avengers scarlet witch the main  villain the one seeking charvez's power  for herself but it dives head first into  the marvel multiverse exploring other  realities that exist in parallel to the  character's own earth-616 unsurprisingly  this comes with some incredibly  crowd-pleasing moments and cameos that  will surely surprise marvel fans of all  ages even if the marketing revealed  professor x and captain carter before  the film even arrived in theaters even  so the scenes in dr strange in the  multiverse of madness that offer up all  that fan service aren't the best in the  movie with sam raimi and the director's  share this time around horror fans are  really in for a treat not only does he  know how to handle superheroes and  heartfelt storytelling thanks to his  work on the spider-man trilogy in the  early 2000s he's also a master at  creating uniquely terrifying scenarios  he's perhaps best known for directing  the evil dead films and he brings some  of his signature camera moves to the  doctor strange sequel one of the key  concepts the movie introduces is the  idea of dreamwalking where a powerful  sorcerer or witch can use the darkhold  to take hold off and control their  alternate selves in another universe  when strange and chavez escaped to the  illuminati's home base of earth 838  scarlett witch from the 616 universe  used his stream walking to control the  wonder maximoff in that universe the  results are chilling the sequence shows  a happier wonder who lives with her two  sons billy and tommy in a quiet suburban  area not unlike west view from one  division it isn't long before sucker mum  wonder realizes she's been hunted by a  supernatural force that follows her  through the house there are glimpses of  the scarlet witch's eyes and reflective  surfaces as well as free-flowing pov  camera shots that swoop through the  house before the villain takes over her  alternate self entirely it doesn't seem  fair it's psychedelic trippy and  downright creepy fans of raymie's work  will love it the trailers for dr strange  and the multiverse of madness heavily  focused on the sequence where the  titular hero meets the illuminati in an  alternate universe likely because of its  fan-pleasing nature yes meeting john  krasinski's mr fantastic is well  fantastic even the return of anson  mounts black bolts is a sight to behold  but it doesn't exactly serve the story  other than as a cautionary tale for  strange the cameos are exciting but they  do feel like an easy bit of fan service  with only marginal story value the  creepy scene in the maximoff house on  the other hand proves that when the mcu  leans into a specific genre it really  excels like it did in phase one iron man  is an action thriller thor is a fantasy  adventure and captain america the first  avenger is a war movie since then the  mcu has mainly stuck to the general  superhero genre with the occasional  diversion into spy thrillers with the  winter soldier or kung 